{
  "id": "01-fabric-vs-power-bi",
  "title": "Fabric vs Power BI",
  "duration": 38.3573,
  "beats": [
    {
      "text": "Microsoft Fabric versus Power BI? Power BI is already inside Fabric.",
      "asset": "architecture",
      "device": "tile",
      "key": "Power BI",
      "start": 0.0,
      "end": 5.088,
      "voice_end": 4.928
    },
    {
      "text": "Power BI handles reports. Fabric covers the workflow around those reports.",
      "asset": "architecture",
      "device": "focus",
      "key": "Microsoft Fabric",
      "start": 5.088,
      "end": 10.0693,
      "voice_end": 9.9093
    },
    {
      "text": "Getting data in. Storing it. Transforming it. Then serving the result.",
      "asset": "onelake",
      "device": "sequence",
      "start": 10.0693,
      "end": 14.24,
      "voice_end": 14.08
    },
    {
      "text": "OneLake gives those workloads a shared, logical data lake.",
      "asset": "onelake",
      "device": "focus",
      "key": "OneLake",
      "start": 14.24,
      "end": 17.856,
      "voice_end": 17.696
    },
    {
      "text": "Direct Lake can read Delta tables without importing an entire copy into the model.",
      "asset": "directlake",
      "device": "focus",
      "key": "Direct Lake",
      "start": 17.856,
      "end": 22.7093,
      "voice_end": 22.5493
    },
    {
      "text": "A Direct Lake refresh still exists. It updates metadata, rather than copying the whole dataset.",
      "asset": "framing",
      "device": "sequence",
      "start": 22.7093,
      "end": 28.5867,
      "voice_end": 28.4267
    },
    {
      "text": "Already know Power BI? Keep it. Add SQL, a lakehouse, and an ingestion pipeline.",
      "asset": "architecture",
      "device": "sequence",
      "start": 28.5867,
      "end": 34.1653,
      "voice_end": 34.0053
    },
    {
      "text": "Start with one end to end workflow. Follow the data into the report.",
      "asset": "onelake",
      "device": "focus",
      "start": 34.1653,
      "end": 38.3573,
      "voice_end": 38.1973
    }
  ],
